{% set local_problem %}
<p>Somerville's rural properties often have unique drainage challenges. Natural grading may direct water toward your home rather than away. Soil conditions vary across larger lots. Properties that have been subdivided or modified over the years may have disrupted natural drainage patterns.</p>

<p>Surface solutions have limits. Splash blocks move water a few inches. Extensions move it a few feet. But on many rural properties, that's not far enough.</p>

<p>Underground drains solve this permanently. Buried pipes carry water far enough away that it can never threaten your home.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Underground drains are buried pipes that connect to your downspouts and carry water to a discharge point far from your home. Rural Somerville properties often have good options for discharge locations — wooded areas, drainage swales, or low points on the property.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've installed underground drainage systems throughout Morgan County for over 20 years. We understand rural properties and what solutions actually work.</p>

<p>We're just 15 minutes away in Hartselle. When we install a system for a Somerville neighbor, we know we'll be around for years to come.</p>
{% endset %}

